        "compat.tools.about.prompt_manager_list": "List prompt presets",
        "compat.tools.about.prompt_manager_apply": "Apply a prompt preset",
        "compat.tools.hover.memory_manager_list": "Lists each memory's id, scene, on/off state and one-line description. Only the ones that would actually be injected by default; all=true adds disabled, inactive-scene and shadowed entries. Read-only.",
        "compat.tools.hover.memory_manager_read": "Reads the full body of one memory by id (<scene>/<name>). The list carries a one-line description only — use this for the body, especially for memories that are off, in an inactive scene, or dropped by the byte budget.",
        "compat.tools.hover.memory_manager_set_enabled": "Flips the index switch only — the .md file is untouched and it is reversible. A disabled memory stops being injected, which frees byte budget for the others; prefer this over deleting when you want to spend fewer tokens.",
        "compat.tools.hover.memory_manager_save": "Creates a memory, or updates the existing one with that id — the receipt says which. Memories enter every later request, so record only what cannot be re-derived from code, config or git — and check the list first for an entry that already says this. Omitted fields are kept; a rename leaves the old file in the trash.",
        "compat.tools.hover.scene_manager_save": "Saves a scene — a named bundle the user enters: whatever its archive lists gets switched on, everything else off. Writing the archive does not turn the scene on; the user enables or enters it on the Scenes page. Sections you omit keep their current value; an empty section means \"switch nothing on\", not \"no restriction\".",
        "compat.tools.hover.mcp_manager_list": "Lists the configured servers, whether each is connected, which tools it exposes, and the note you wrote for it. Servers that connected before but not now are marked — that means this one is broken, not unconfigured. tools=true also lists each server's tool names, marking the switched-off ones (off); a server that is off only has the names recorded from its last run.",
        "compat.tools.hover.mcp_manager_switch": "action=on/off enables or disables a whole server; pass `tool` to switch just that one tool (a disabled tool disappears from the model-visible tool table and is blocked at execution, and it survives a DSH restart); action=restart disables the server, waits for it to drop, then enables it back the way it was — use it after a config change or when a server is stuck. Pass level when the same server name exists at both project and global level.",
        "compat.tools.hover.mcp_manager_save": "Adds a server (streamable-http or stdio) or updates the one with that name — the receipt says which. When updating, every field you omit keeps its current value, so changing one URL does not mean restating the whole config (and the secrets survive); for stdio, command+args is the command the host actually spawns, and changing it raises a confirmation card. Only on the user's explicit request.",
        "compat.tools.hover.skill_manager_list": "Lists each skill's on/off state, whether it wins or is shadowed, and its source path. The always-on catalog carries names and summaries only — use this to see what you turned off and which copy of a name wins; all=true includes disabled and shadowed copies.",
        "compat.tools.hover.skill_manager_read": "Reads one skill's SKILL.md body by name (the catalog has names and summaries only). Name collisions resolve to the copy actually in effect; pass root to inspect a shadowed copy instead. Not sent in conversations where the official skill tool is mounted.",
        "compat.tools.hover.skill_manager_set_enabled": "Toggles by skill name or by source directory. Disabled skills leave the catalog and cannot be loaded; when a name exists in several roots only the winning copy counts, so enabling the wrong one changes nothing.",
        "compat.tools.hover.skill_manager_save": "Creates a skill, or updates the copy this plugin wrote itself — the receipt says which. It lands in hub (tool-management/skills/), matching the panel's \"Create skill\"; a new skill starts disabled, so enable it before use, and skills living in the official roots are never touched. The catalog is injected into every request, so make the description say when to use it.",
        "compat.tools.hover.subagent_manager_list": "Lists the available personas (pre-configured subagent roles) with their descriptions. The always-on catalog carries the same list; this tool always returns the current, complete version — including conversations the catalog does not reach.",
        "compat.tools.hover.subagent_manager_run": "Hands a task to a named persona: it gets the persona as its own system prompt, works in its own context and returns only the final result. With inherit it also sees this conversation's finished turns. It spends real tokens and asks the user by default.",
        "compat.tools.hover.subagent_manager_set_enabled": "A disabled persona leaves the catalog and cannot be delegated to; personas bound to a scene are enabled automatically when that scene is entered.",
        "compat.tools.hover.subagent_manager_save": "Creates a persona, or updates the existing one — the receipt says which. You can set the name, description, body (the body becomes the subagent's system prompt) and output contract; omitted fields keep their current values, and a rename makes scene and archive bindings follow. Provider, model and tool limits stay in the panel (the model cannot tell whether it got them right, so it is not offered them). The description decides when the model picks it.",
        "compat.tools.hover.prompt_manager_list": "Lists the prompt presets with their summaries and marks the one currently in effect — only one is active at a time. Use it to confirm the name before switching.",
        "compat.tools.hover.prompt_manager_apply": "Applies a preset to the user-level AGENTS.md; later conversations follow it immediately. Only one preset is in effect, so applying another replaces it.",
